* text=auto eol=lf

# Paradox script and localization are LF + UTF-8. Both also carry a BOM in this
# mod, but only one of the two is checked: `has_bom` has a single call site, in
# `_check_loc_file`, which is reached only for a .yml under localization/. The
# BOM on every script .txt here is a convention NOTHING ENFORCES: a .txt that
# has lost one still passes `ck3.py validate`. NOTHING HERE PRESERVES A BOM
# EITHER: `text` governs line endings only, and a CRLF checkout would not strip
# a BOM. The two are recorded together because they are easy to conflate, not
# because they are checked together.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. The box this mod is written on has
# core.autocrlf=true, so without a declaration here every checkout writes CRLF
# into files the parent tooling repo declares LF. The parent's .gitattributes
# does not reach this far: an attributes lookup stops at the top level of the
# repository that contains the file, and this mod is its own repository. It went
# unnoticed because git cleans CRLF back to LF on the way in, so `git status`
# reads clean over a working tree that is mixed - and it was mixed, in a
# minority of the files under common/.
*.txt text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.gui text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.dds binary
*.tga binary
